[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The recommended dosage regimen for Lopinavir-Ritonavir is as follows: In adults, it can be administered as a once-daily regimen of 800 mg/200 mg (10 mL oral solution) or a twice-daily regimen of 400 mg/100 mg (5 mL oral solution). The once-daily regimen is not recommended for patients with three or more lopinavir resistance-associated substitutions, those taking certain concomitant medications (e.g., carbamazepine, phenobarbital, phenytoin, efavirenz, nevirapine, nelfinavir), pediatric patients under 18, or pregnant women. When twice-daily Lopinavir-Ritonavir is co-administered with efavirenz, nevirapine, or nelfinavir, the dose must be increased to 520 mg/130 mg (6.5 mL). In pregnant women with no lopinavir-associated resistance, the recommended dose is 400 mg/100 mg twice daily; once-daily dosing and the oral solution formulation should be avoided in pregnancy. In pediatric patients, once-daily dosing is not recommended, and dosing should be calculated based on weight or BSA to avoid underdosing. It is also not recommended in neonates before a postmenstrual age of 42 weeks and postnatal age of 14 days has been attained.",
