[?2004l[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "Important warnings and precautions associated with Lopinavir-Ritonavir include: 1) Risk of serious and potentially fatal adverse reactions due to CYP3A-mediated drug interactions. 2) Toxicity in preterm neonates caused by ethanol and propylene glycol excipients in the oral solution, which has resulted in fatal cardiac toxicity, renal failure, and respiratory complications. 3) Pancreatitis (sometimes fatal), especially in patients with marked triglyceride elevations. 4) Hepatotoxicity, including transaminase elevations and hepatic dysfunction, particularly in patients with underlying chronic hepatitis B or C or cirrhosis. 5) QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes, necessitating avoidance in patients with congenital long QT syndrome or hypokalemia. 6) PR interval prolongation, which can lead to second or third-degree atrioventricular block, requiring caution in patients with structural heart disease or conduction system abnormalities.",
