[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "Important warnings and precautions associated with Paxlovid include: 1) Risk of serious, life-threatening, or fatal adverse reactions due to drug interactions with medications metabolized by CYP3A, or loss of therapeutic effect and viral resistance due to strong CYP3A inducers. 2) Hypersensitivity reactions, including anaphylaxis and serious skin reactions such as toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN) and Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS), which require immediate discontinuation of the drug. 3) Hepatotoxicity, characterized by hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice, requiring caution in patients with pre-existing liver disease or enzyme abnormalities. 4) Risk of HIV-1 resistance development to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection, due to the co-administration of ritonavir.",
