[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The safety risks listed for Paxlovid include: 1) Serious, life-threatening, or fatal adverse reactions resulting from significant drug-drug interactions due to ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, and potential loss of therapeutic efficacy or resistance due to CYP3A inducers. 2) Hypersensitivity reactions, including anaphylaxis and serious skin conditions such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS) and toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN). 3) Hepatotoxicity, including clinical hepatitis, jaundice, and hepatic transaminase elevations, necessitating caution in patients with pre-existing liver disease or liver enzyme abnormalities. 4) Risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection, because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir.",
